{
  "_doc": "Minimap bake inputs (Update 04 section 1, DECISIONS T-065), read by tools_src/bake_minimap.gd. The list of maps that must have map data comes from MapCatalog (the campaign chain + the B&S star map), not from here: a map with no row here bakes with 'defaults' (one floor covering every height, the style of its game). floors: bottom to top; y_min/y_max = the band of the player's feet that counts as this floor; base_y = its floor height (uv_to_world); cut = the height the orthographic camera slices the level at (walls cut there read as walls, anything above is left out); depth = how far below the band the render reaches (m, default 0.6); zones = zone ids whose boxes limit the floor in XZ (the floor's 'rects'; outside them the image is empty and floor_at falls back to an unlimited floor); mask_zones (+ mask_grow m) = limit only the image, not floor_at (Kaltenbrunn's surface hides the chapel vaults below the snow). zone_names: labels for the zone ids (else the map's own json zone names, else the id). exclude: node-name fragments the bake never draws (sky, water planes, light cards). connectors are found automatically (stairs / ramps by StaticBody name, lifts, the map json's climb_links); extra_connectors adds hand-placed ones.",
